giorgia investigators this morning are  looking into the deadly shooting of a  Georgia Tech student on campus scout  Shultz was a 21 year old senior majoring  in engineering Schultz identified as  either male nor female and was president  of the school's pride alliance Georgia  Tech police responded to a call Saturday  night that led to Schultz's death  encounter was captured on cell phone  video  mark Strassmann is at the University in  Atlanta with the questions over officers  use of force mark good morning good  morning scout Schultz was shot right on  this Street around midnight on Saturday  a student killed by university police  right on campus those officers were  responding to a call about a man  carrying a gun and a knife when this  happened video you can see scout Schultz  walking toward police holding what they  believe was a pocket knife you can hear  the 21 year old student call out to them  Schultz paused before stepping toward an  officer who gave a final warning the  officer then opened fire with a single  fatal shot  Schultz died shortly after at a nearby  hospital pictures of the scene show this  small multi-purpose tool on the ground  the blade of the knife inside it was  folded Schultz had no gun in an  interview with the Atlanta  journal-constitution Schultz's mother  Lynn Schultz questioned why police  didn't use pepper spray or Tasers  she said Schulz attempted suicide two  years ago Chris Stewart the family's  lawyer told the newspaper he believes  Schultz was having a mental breakdown  and didn't know what to do  Stewart added that he doesn't believe  Schultz wanted to die in what's known as  suicide by cop but they should have had  a non-lethal option Julia gray was  friends with Schulz both belonged to the  campus LGBTQ community Scout was the one  out there marching Scout was the one  that showed an endless amount of pride  for who they were  Schultz identified as non-binary meaning  neither male nor female and was the  president of Georgia Tech's pride  Alliance no one should get to that point  where they they feel that way especially  when they don't want to hurt anyone  Scout didn't want to hurt though anyone  students have started a memorial to  Schulz er over my shoulder as you can  see state investigators are leading the  official look into this fatal shooting  we asked them whether responding  officers carried mace or a stun gun but  they had no further details for us  people are raising that question as well  mark a lot of questions in that case  thank you very much
 

